<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9081" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">col-lĭno</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conl-</span></b> ), lēvi, lĭtum,
		3, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to besmear</i>, <i>to cover over</i>,
				<i>defile</i>, <i>pollute</i>:
			aliquid, aliquā re (rare; not in class. prose).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ora venenis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. R. Am. 351</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tabulas cerā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 17, 9, 17</span></i>
			: crines adulteros pulvere, * <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 1,
				15, 20</span></i> (cf. <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 12, 99</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">foedare in pulvere crines): caeno collitus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Poen. 4, 2, 4</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pulchrum ornatum turpes mores pejus caeno
					collinunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Most. 1, 3, 133</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Poen. 1, 2, 96</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
